@strong{@anchor{Exercise 4.54}Exercise 4.54:} The original book implements
@code{require} as an ordinary procedure that uses @code{amb}, to be defined by
the user as part of a nondeterministic program.  In this edition @code{amb}
always has two alternatives, so there is no @code{amb} with no alternatives to
fail with, and @code{require} must be a special form.  This requires a new
clause in the dispatch of the evaluator that recognizes @code{require} at the
head of an application.  Complete the following clause, which evaluates the
condition and handles the two outcomes.

